# What the build context may NOT see.
#
# This is a security control before it is a speed one. Every file sent to the
# daemon can end up in a layer, and a layer is permanent: deleting a file in a
# later instruction leaves it fully readable in the image history, so
# `docker history` or an unpacked tarball still yields it. The only reliable
# way to keep a secret out of an image is to keep it out of the context.

# Secrets. `.env` holds the database URL, the cookie and CSRF secrets, and two
# Ed25519 private keys. `!.env.example` because that one is deliberately
# placeholder-only and is useful inside the image as documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host-built native modules. argon2 and sharp compile per platform; copying a
# Windows or macOS build into a Linux image produces a module that loads and
# then fails at runtime. The image installs its own.
node_modules

# Build output, rebuilt inside the image from source.
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Git history. Carries every previously committed value, including any secret
# that was later removed.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Tests, coverage and tooling: none of it runs in the final image, and each
# file is attack surface plus bytes.
test
coverage
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
jest.config.*
.eslintrc*
eslint.config.mjs
.prettierrc*

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch.
*.log
logs
tmp
